<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-Boliden sale lifts Trelleborg H1.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Boliden sale lifts Trelleborg H1.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish mining and rubber group Trelleborg on Tuesday posted its results for the six months ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,003 vs    657</p>
<p> Capital gain from Boliden spinoff   1,463 vs     -</p>
<p> Turnover				   11,817 vs 10,535</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		13.40 vs   4.05</p>
<p> Costs of goods sold		     9,350 vs  8,356</p>
<p> Admin, sales costs			1,838 vs  1,461</p>
<p> Other income/costs		 CREDIT  19 vs     27 CHARGE</p>
<p> Associate interests			  85 vs     52</p>
<p> Operating profit			    733 vs    563</p>
<p> Restructuring costs (incl cap gain) 1,304 vs    nil</p>
<p> Net financial items		CHARGE  34 vs     94 CREDIT</p>
<p> Tax					     417 vs    182</p>
<p> Minorities				     11 vs    nil</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,575 vs    475</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found expectations of a profit after financial items of 2.16 billion crowns for the first half of 1997 including a capital gain of about 1.5 billion crowns from selling shares in mining unit Boliden.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
